Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/ggplot2/c/x72iesZuD9c/m/NWVOz-dCphIJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Currently geom_density creates a closed polygon (plotted in red
below); is there any way to make it a single line as in the normal
density function (plotted in green below)?

a = data.frame(obs = test_data,condition = 'None')
p = ggplot(
	data = a
	,aes(
		x = obs
	)
)+geom_histogram(
	aes(
		y = ..density..
		)
)+geom_density(
	colour='red'
)+stat_function(
	fun = dnorm
	,args = list(
		m=mean(a$obs)
		,sd=sd(a$obs)
	)
	,colour = 'green'
)

--
