Dear all,

I'm facing a minor aesthetic challenge in the attached graph.

load("d.rda")
dl <- subset(d2, a0 == "3" &  ar %in% c(1, 1.6, 2.2))

p <-
ggplot(data = subset(d2, ar < 2.4), mapping = aes(x = value, y = int))+
stat_smooth( method = "lm", colour="grey") +
scale_shape("polarisation\naxis",labels=c("long", "short"),  solid=F)+
geom_point(mapping=aes(shape=factor(variable), colour=a0))+
geom_text(data=dl,hjust=1.5, vjust=0, size=2,
mapping=aes(label=factor(ar), colour=a0))+
scale_x_continuous(breaks=10^-seq(8, 4, by=-1), trans="log10",
expression(paste(V/L, " (", mu*m^3, ")"))) +
scale_y_continuous(breaks=10^-seq(7, 3, by=-1),trans="log10",
	expression(integral(sigma[ext]*(lambda)*d*lambda,0, infinity )* "
("*mu*m^3*")")) +
scale_colour_brewer("equ. radius\n / nm", palette="Set1")+theme_bw()

p

I'd like to specify symbol shapes that vary as "ar", but for each
shape there would be a hollow symbol for variable =="long" and a full
symbol for variable == "short". Hope this makes sense...

Best wishes,

baptiste

